    "result_text": "Both findings addressed; tests remain green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n**Finding 1 (agreed) \u2014 duplicated per-line canonicalization.** Extracted the normalize\u2192null policy into `OwnerAddress.normalizeToNull(String)`, now the single home for the \"blank line stored as null\" rule. Both `ValidateNewOwner` (create) and `ApplyOwner` (update) reduce to the three symmetric calls, so the policy can no longer drift between the two paths.\n\n**Finding 2 (agreed) \u2014 `compose(...)` visibility.** Made `compose(...)` `private`; it's only called by `effective(...)` within the same class. The helper's package-private \"either-form\" surface is now just `effective` / `normalize` / `normalizeToNull`.\n\nNo behavioural change \u2014 the refactor is purely structural, and the acceptance suite (structured-address composition + flat-address backward compatibility) still passes.",
