    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is largely well-placed: centralizing the address derivation in `OwnerAddress.effective(...)` and writing the canonical value back into the request/entity (so downstream readers of `getAddress()` are untouched) fits this codebase's established \"single source of truth + write canonical form back\" pattern (telephone, email, `RegistrationDates`). The schema/DB/OpenAPI additions are consistent and additive. One structural issue, plus a minor note:\n\n**1. The structured-address handling is duplicated across `ValidateNewOwner` (create) and `ApplyOwner` (update), including the empty\u2192null policy.**\n\nBoth classes do the same three-part sequence:\n```java\nString normalizedLine1 = OwnerAddress.normalize(request.getAddressLine1());\nString normalizedLine2 = OwnerAddress.normalize(request.getAddressLine2());\ntarget.setAddressLine1(normalizedLine1.isEmpty() ? null : normalizedLine1);\ntarget.setAddressLine2(normalizedLine2.isEmpty() ? null : normalizedLine2);\ntarget.setAddress(OwnerAddress.effective(\n        request.getAddressLine1(), request.getAddressLine2(), request.getAddress()));\n```\nThe `ApplyOwner` comment even flags it (\"mirroring the create path\"). `OwnerAddress` is documented as the single source of truth \"so [the stored/returned value] can never drift apart\" \u2014 yet the `normalize(...)` \u2192 `isEmpty() ? null` rule for each line now lives inline in two files. If that policy changes (e.g. store `\"\"` instead of `null`, or trim differently), both steps must change in lockstep \u2014 exactly the drift these helpers exist to prevent.\n\nActionable fix: give `OwnerAddress` the normalize-to-null decision, e.g. `static String normalizeToNull(String line)`, so both callers reduce to:\n```java\ntarget.setAddressLine1(OwnerAddress.normalizeToNull(request.getAddressLine1()));\ntarget.setAddressLine2(OwnerAddress.normalizeToNull(request.getAddressLine2()));\ntarget.setAddress(OwnerAddress.effective(\n        request.getAddressLine1(), request.getAddressLine2(), request.getAddress()));\n```\n(The differing targets \u2014 `OwnerFieldsDto` vs `Owner` \u2014 prevent collapsing the whole block into one helper, but the per-line canonicalization is the extractable, duplicated kernel.)\n\n**2. Minor:** `OwnerAddress.compose(...)` is package-private with full javadoc but is only called by `effective(...)` within the same class. Unless it's intended as part of the helper's public contract, making it `private` would keep the \"either-form\" API surface to just `effective`/`normalize` and avoid implying an external caller that doesn't exist.",
